  "body": {
    "id": "thm:envelope-iff",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every \\(\\mathcal M\\subseteq\\mathcal G^{\\mathrm{WARP}}_3\\) with \\(\\mathcal S_3\\subseteq\\mathcal M\\), the vector \\((\\mu_t^\\star)_{t\\in\\mathcal B}\\) is outcome-nonrestrictively identified on \\(\\mathcal M\\) if and only if \\(\\mathcal M\\subseteq\\mathcal E_3\\). Consequently \\(\\mathcal E_3\\) is the unique inclusion-maximal such support. Relative to the coordinate-separable support \\(\\mathcal S_3\\) of Blackwell and Pashley, this strictly enlarges the admissible response family from eight to 29 maps while preserving the same eight perfect-complier means.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\mathcal M",
      "\\mathcal G^{\\mathrm{WARP}}_3",
      "\\mathcal S_3",
      "\\mu_t^\\star",
      "t",
      "\\mathcal B",
      "\\mathcal E_3"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:positive-perfect-share",
      "ass:support-in-model",
      "ass:separable-baseline",
      "def:warp-class",
      "def:separable-family",
      "def:null-envelope",
      "def:outcome-nonrestrictive-id",
      "lem:mobius-coefficients",
